# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**AI assistance inside the applications you already run.** A gateway role, *svc-ai-litellm*, fronts OpenAI, Anthropic and OpenRouter from declared keys, with *svc-ai-ollama* and the new *svc-ai-lmstudio* serving local models from one shared catalogue, so inference can stay inside the deployment. Sixteen applications use it for their own built-in AI features instead of calling a vendor directly: WordPress AI Engine, MediaWiki AIEditingAssistant, Moodle's AI subsystem, Zammad Smart Assist, the xWiki LLM extension, Discourse AI, the Matrix ChatGPT bridge, Nextcloud, Mattermost Agents, n8n, Open WebUI and Flowise. The gateway's admin UI signs in through Keycloak. See [svc-ai-litellm](roles/svc-ai-litellm/README.md) and [svc-ai-lmstudio](roles/svc-ai-lmstudio/README.md)."
msgstr "**AI pagalba jau vykdomose programose.** Vartų funkcija, *svc-ai-litellm*, frontai OpenAI, Anthropic ir OpenRouter iš paskelbtų raktų, su *svc-ai-ollama* ir naujas *svc-ai-lmstudio* tarnauti vietinius modelius iš vieno bendro katalogo, todėl išvada gali likti viduje diegimo. Šešiolika programų naudoti jį savo built- in AI funkcijas, o ne skambinti pardavėjui tiesiogiai: WordPress AI variklis, MediaWiki AIEditingAssistant MoodlePG posistemis, Zammad Smart Assist, xWiki LLM pratęsimo, Discourse PG, Matrix ChatGPT tiltas, Nextcloud, Mattermost Agentai, n8n, Open WebUI ir Flowise. Vartai admin UI pasirašo per Keycloak- Matai. [svc-ai-litellm](roles/svc-ai-litellm/README.md) ir [svc-ai-lmstudio](roles/svc-ai-lmstudio/README.md)."

