# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tool categories exposed at the pinned version cover issues and work items, merge requests (including diffs and conflicts), pipelines and jobs, labels, project and group search, repository files and commits, and instance metadata. The set includes mutating tools (``create_merge_request``, ``create_workitem_note``, ``link_work_items``). GitLab enforces no server-side read-only mode: the ``mcp`` scope grants both read and create access, and the only restriction mechanism is the per-request ``X-Gitlab-Enabled-Mcp-Server-Tools`` header, which the clients in this repository do not send. ``mcp.tools.read_only_default`` and ``mcp.tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` are declarative metadata, not an enforced policy. Every tool call runs with the blast radius of the ``root`` account."
msgstr "Įrankių kategorijos veikiami ne prisegimo versija apima klausimus ir darbo elementus, sujungti prašymus (įskaitant difuzijas ir konfliktus), vamzdynai ir darbo vietos, etiketės, projektų ir grupių paieška, saugyklos failus ir įsipareigoja, ir pavyzdžiui metaduomenys. Rinkinyje yra mutacijos įrankiai (``create_merge_request``, ``create_workitem_note``, ``link_work_items``). GitLab užtikrina ne server- side read- only režimas: ``mcp`` taikymo sritis suteikia tiek skaityti ir sukurti prieigą, ir vienintelis apribojimo mechanizmas yra ``X-Gitlab-Enabled-Mcp-Server-Tools`` antraštė, kurios šios saugyklos klientai nesiunčia. ``mcp.tools.read_only_default`` ir ``mcp.tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` yra deklaratyvūs metaduomenys, o ne vykdoma politika. Kiekvienas įrankis skambutis vyksta su sprogimo spindulys ``root`` sąskaita."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tool categories exposed at the pinned version cover issues and work items, merge requests (including diffs and conflicts), pipelines and jobs, labels, project and group search, repository files and commits, and instance metadata. The set includes mutating tools (`create_merge_request`, `create_workitem_note`, `link_work_items`). GitLab enforces no server-side read-only mode: the `mcp` scope grants both read and create access, and the only restriction mechanism is the per-request `X-Gitlab-Enabled-Mcp-Server-Tools` header, which the clients in this repository do not send. `mcp.tools.read_only_default` and `mcp.tools.mutating_tools_enabled` are declarative metadata, not an enforced policy. Every tool call runs with the blast radius of the `root` account."
