msgid "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` resolves the caller's token through `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` and presents it as the Bearer"
msgstr "`ToolServerConnection.auth_type: system_oauth` Išsprendžia skambinančiojo simbolį per `oauth_manager.get_oauth_token(user.id, oauth_session_id)` ir pristato jį kaip nešėjas"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Unit tests` verify isolated logic."
msgstr "`Unit tests` tikrinti izoliuotą logiką."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`UsersLookup` yields the `no-reply` user dict used to derive `from` and `password`. Missing entries MUST yield an empty dict. The fallback for `from` is then `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`."
msgstr "`UsersLookup` išveda `no-reply` naudotojo diktas, naudojamas išvesti `from` ir `password`. Trūkstami įrašai PRIVALO duoti tuščią įrašą. Atgalinė `from` tada `root@<inventory_hostname>.localdomain`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ is a powerful source code editor with a wide plugin ecosystem, supporting development workflows across many languages and platforms. See also the `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ and general `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ on Wikipedia."
msgstr "`Visual Studio Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ yra galingas kodo redaktorius su plačiu įskiepiai ekosistemos, remti plėtros darbų srautus per daugelį kalbų ir platformų. Taip pat žr. `Arch Wiki - Development Tools <https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Category:Development>`__ ir apskritai `Software Engineering <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_engineering>`__ Vikipedijoje."

# translation-refused: libretranslate protected-span
