msgstr "``name``: unikalus kartografavimo ID"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``networks.internet.dns`` arrives through ``-e @inventories/...`` and is read straight out of ``variables``, which hands back whatever the file contains. While that was a literal address nobody noticed; an expression there reached the daemon as its own source text and docker refused the config with ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."
msgstr "``networks.internet.dns`` Atvyksta per ``-e @inventories/...`` ir skaityti tiesiai iš ``variables``, kuri rankas atgal, kad ir ką failas yra. Nors tai buvo pažodinis adresas niekas nepastebėjo; posakis ten pasiekė demoną kaip savo pradinio teksto ir dokeris atsisakė konfig ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``new_text_or_None`` is ``None`` when nothing changed."
msgstr "``new_text_or_None`` yra ``None`` kai niekas nepasikeitė."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``nfs``            NFS opt-in (bool or dict), ``None`` if absent"
msgstr "``nfs`` @ item: inlistbox (bool arba dict), ``None`` jei nėra"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``noqa`` and ``nocheck`` are accepted as synonyms (case-insensitive) by this parser. By repo convention every project rule from ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUST use ``nocheck:`` because ``# noqa: <code>`` is also parsed by ruff as a flake8 directive and triggers ``invalid-noqa-code`` warnings on every project-specific rule key. ``noqa:`` is reserved for real flake8 / ruff codes (``E402``, ``F401``, …). The ``direct-yaml`` lint enforces the convention by hard-rejecting the ``noqa:`` form."
msgstr "``noqa`` ir ``nocheck`` priimami kaip sinonimai (nejautrus) šis analizatorius. Pagal atpirkimo susitarimą kiekvienas projekto taisyklė nuo ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` PRIE ``nocheck:`` kadangi: ``# noqa: <code>`` taip pat perskaito gruff kaip flake8 Direktyva ir priežastys ``invalid-noqa-code`` perspėjimai apie kiekvieną konkretų projekto taisyklių raktą. ``noqa:`` yra skirtas nekilnojamojo flake8 / antriniai kodai (``E402``, ``F401``,...). ``direct-yaml`` Konventą įgyvendina griežtai atmesdama ``noqa:`` forma."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``offset`` moves that start deliberately: it is how an operator reaches the tail without waiting for anything. It defaults to 0, so every run that does not ask for it deploys the same head and can be compared against the last one. This used to be derived from the sweep number instead, which bought tail coverage at the price of the head -- chunk 0 began wherever the arithmetic pointed, the rows that matter most ran only every few sweeps, and no two runs were comparable."
msgstr "``offset`` judesius, kad pradėti sąmoningai: kaip operatorius pasiekia uodegą nieko nelaukdamas. Jis neįvykdo įsipareigojimų 0, todėl kiekvienas bėgimas, kuris neprašo ji dislokuoja tą pačią galvą ir gali būti lyginamas su paskutiniu. Tai buvo išvesta iš nuvalyto skaičiaus, kuris nupirko uodegos padengimą už galvos kainą -- 0 pradėjo kur aritmetinis smailės, eilutės, kad matyt labiausiai vyko tik kas keletą sweeps, ir nė du bėgimai buvo palyginami."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc-authenticator`` and ``ldap-authenticator`` are mutually exclusive auth backends (only one may be enabled; see ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` carries only the installer coordinate."
msgstr "``oidc-authenticator`` ir ``ldap-authenticator`` yra tarpusavyje nesuderinamos auth realizacijos (gali būti įjungtas tik vienas; žr. ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` turi tik montuotojo koordinates."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc``: baseline admin OIDC round-trip plus the three RBAC scenarios (subscriber/editor/administrator)."
msgstr "``oidc``: pradinis admin OIDC žiedinė kelionė plius trys RBAC scenarijai (subscriber/editor/administrator)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``openssl_conf_host`` (string): host path for generated openssl.cnf"
msgstr "``openssl_conf_host`` (eilutė): generuotas mazgo kelias openssl.cnf"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``out`` itself lives under the dump dir (both derive from INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), so the walk must skip its own output subtree or copytree recurses into the growing destination until ENAMETOOLONG."
msgstr "``out`` pati gyvena po sąvartynu (ir INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), todėl pėsčiomis turi praleisti savo produkcijos submedį arba autorinis medis atsitraukia į auginimo paskirties iki ENAMETOOLONG."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the branch lives on."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` filialas gyvena toliau."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the run lives in."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` bėgimas gyvuoja."

